<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theophilos (emperor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 812–842</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theophilos was Byzantine emperor from 829 to 842, of the Amorian dynasty, and the last emperor to support iconoclasm. He fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a>, who sacked Amorion in 838, and sought allies against them, exchanging embassies with the Umayyad emir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-ii">Abd al-Rahman II</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. He was a patron of building and learning in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>; after his death his widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodora-wife-of-theophilos">Theodora</a> restored the veneration of icons in 843.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theophilos-emperor.jpg" alt="Theophilos (emperor)" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Skylitzes · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Theophilos_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
